#. max 1999 bytes
msgctxt "1"
msgid "That which symbolizes Gilgamesh's youth.\nIt represents his quest for immortality and why.\n\n             ◆\n\nAnd so, that childhood of his came to an end.\nThe tyrant that shed neither blood nor tears.\nThe hero who enjoyed himself, indulging in every treasure,\nevery pleasure.\n\nA king with the conviction to commit good and evil alike.\nSince the absolute standard is \"himself,\"\nhe has no need for other ideologies or ways of life.\nHis conceit is equal to the Macedonian King of Conquerors,\nbut the main difference between the King of Heroes and\nthe King of Conquerors is that he \"does not need vassals.\"\n\nThis hero, from beginning to end, ruled only \"himself.\"\nWhat he loved were simply treasures, tools;\npeople were only things fated to disappear.\n\n……even if he recognized\nhow much they deserved to be loved.\n\n             ◆\n\nThe themes in \"CCC\" make talking about women unavoidable.\nThis is a tangent, but Gilgamesh's preferred type is\n\"a noble #RUBS  maiden#RUBEvirgin#REND.\"\n(As a child, his type was \"a flower blooming in the wild.\")\nIt seems he hates women who, while reliant on men,\nare using them on the inside.\n"
msgstr ""

